#!args scenario=Scenario_Debug_USA seed=42
#
# Regression: a scenario's `initialHandCards` must actually reach that faction's opening hand, and
# must count towards the seven rather than be dealt on top of it.
#
# Two separate bugs, both surfaced by ShuffleDecks:
#
#   1. DeckState.DrawCardByName ran FindIndex over DeckCardStates and fed the result into
#      DeckCardIds[index]. DeckCardStates is CardState.ForIds(DeckCardIds), which filters the master
#      CardStatesById dictionary and so comes back in card-id order, not deck order. That only ever
#      worked because ids were handed out in deck declaration order and nothing reordered the deck;
#      ShuffleDecks now permutes DeckCardIds just before PlaceCards, so the index pointed at an
#      unrelated card. The id was still valid, so the -1 "not found" path never fired and nothing was
#      logged: the named card quietly stayed in the deck and a random one went to hand instead.
#
#   2. GameFlow.StartGame drew a flat 7 after the scenario cards were already in hand, so a faction
#      opened with 7 + N and had to dump the surplus at its first DISCARD step. It now draws *to* 7,
#      the same as DrawStepHandlerDefault does every later turn.
#
# Scenario_Debug_USA gives GERMANY two initialHandCards and every other faction none.
#
# The ids below are pinned to the seed in the #!args line — with the deck shuffled, which copy of a
# duplicated card (Germany holds several Sea Battles) DrawCardByName reaches first is seed-dependent.
# What they are really checking is that these two specific cards are in hand at all: with bug 1 both
# sit in the deck, and with bug 2 the hand is 9.
# Run:  tests/run-cli.sh tests/qgc/scenario_initial_hand_cards.qgc

prompt                                  # turn 1, Germany, PLAY_CARD

# Drawn TO seven, not seven on top of the two scenario cards. FAILS (9) with bug 2.
assert handsize GERMANY == 7

assert card 41 in hand                  # Ardennes Offensive  — FAILS ("deck") with bug 1
assert card 18 in hand                  # Sea Battle          — FAILS ("deck") with bug 1

# A faction with an empty initialHandCards list is unaffected: still a plain opening seven.
assert handsize UNITED_KINGDOM == 7

quit
